2. Adjusting the synthesis temperature: The synthesis temperature can affect the crystal size, morphology, and stability of zeolites. Higher temperatures can lead to larger crystal sizes and more stable structures, while lower temperatures can result in smaller crystals and more amorphous structures.

3. Adjusting the synthesis pressure: The synthesis pressure can affect the rate of nucleation and growth of zeolite crystals. Higher pressures can lead to faster nucleation and growth, while lower pressures can result in slower nucleation and growth.

4. Adjusting the synthesis time: The synthesis time can affect the crystal size and morphology of zeolites. Longer synthesis times can lead to larger crystal sizes and more uniform morphologies, while shorter times can result in smaller clusters and less uniform morphologies.

