\[
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} f(t) e^{-i\omega t} \, dt = \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} \left( 3\sin(2\pi t) + 2\cos(4\pi t) \right) e^{-i\omega t} \, dt
\]

We can split this into two integrals:

\[
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} 3\sin(2\pi t) e^{-i\omega t} \, dt + \int_{-\infty}^{\infty} 2\cos(4\pi t) e^{-i\omega t} \, dt
\]

