\[
\Delta \eta = F_{\text{fr}} v
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}
\]
This is derived from the thermodynamic inequality:
\[
\Delta S > \frac{\Delta \eta}{T}
\]
For a process involving friction, the entropy increases, and the entropy change is:
\[
\Delta S = \frac{\Delta \eta}{T} + \frac{\Delta \eta}{T} = \frac{2\Delta \eta}{T}
\]
The entropy production rate is:
\[
\pi_S = \frac{\Delta \eta}{T} = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\boxed{\frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T}}
