</USER_REQUEST>

<GROUND_TRUTH>
To calculate the body-to-source voltage (\(V_{BS}\)) required to shift the threshold voltage (\(V_T\)) by \(-1.0\) V, we use the body effect formula for a p-channel MOSFET:

\[
\Delta V_T = \gamma \left( \sqrt{|2\phi_F + V_{BS}|} - \sqrt{|2\phi_F|} \right)
\]

Where:
- \(\Delta V_T = -1.0 \text{ V}\) (desired shift in threshold voltage)
- \(\gamma\) is the body effect coefficient
- \(\phi_F\) is the Fermi potential

#### Step 1: Calculate the Fermi potential (\(\phi_F\))
For an n-type substrate (\(N_d = 10^{16} \text{ cm}^{-3}\)):

\[
\phi_F = \frac{kT}{q} \ln\left(\frac{N_d}{n_i}\right)
\]

