ADP + Pi

The standard free energy change for this reaction (ΔG°) can be calculated using the standard free energy change for the reaction of ADP + Pi = ATP:

ΔG° (ATP hydrolysis) = -ΔG° (ADP + Pi = ATP)

Since the standard free energy change for the reaction ADP + Pi = ATP is -30.5 kJ/mol, we can plug this into the equation:

ΔG° (ATP hydrolysis) = -(-30.5 kJ/mol) = 30.5 kJ/mol

